# Infrathon launch configuration — copy to launch/mlsysforge.env and edit.
#
#   cp launch/mlsysforge.env.example launch/mlsysforge.env
#
# Every key here is the real environment variable name. A value is applied
# only when that variable is not already set, so precedence is:
#
#   command-line flag  >  environment  >  this file  >  built-in default
#
# Pick this file up automatically by placing it at launch/mlsysforge.env, or
# point at another path with `--config FILE` or `MLSYSFORGE_CONFIG=FILE`.
# A flat JSON object with the same keys works too (launch/mlsysforge.json).
# Unknown keys are rejected at launch, so a typo fails loudly.


########################################
# Required on every host
########################################

# Where saved candidate versions are written. Create the store with a
# `.sforge-version-store.json` marker file:
#   {"schema_version": 1, "kind": "sforge-version-store", "store_id": "<name>"}
# and register each task as <store>/tasks/<task-directory>/task.json:
#   {"schema_version": 1, "task_directory": "<dir>", "task_id": "<id>"}
# Launches fail closed when the store does not register the task being run.
SFORGE_VERSION_STORE_ROOT=/path/to/agent-task-version-submit

# Infrathon assets (tasks/latest/<task>/assets/fetch.sh puts them here) and this host's
# hardware type (h100-94gb-400w or h100-80gb-700w; detected from GPU 0 when unset).
INFRATHON_ASSETS_ROOT=/home/YOU/.cache/infrathon/assets
#INFRATHON_HARDWARE=h100-80gb-700w
#HF_HUB_CACHE=/home/YOU/.cache/huggingface/hub

# Host directory holding node + one agent CLI, built by:
#   launch/build-agent-runtime.sh --agent codex --version 0.159.3
# Task work images are agent-free and bind-mount it read-only. Optional: the
# launchers default to <clone>/../agent_runtimes/<agent>-<pinned version>, where
# build-agent-runtime.sh puts it. Set it only for a runtime elsewhere; it then
# applies to every --agent.
#SFORGE_AGENT_RUNTIME_DIR=/path/to/agent_runtimes/codex-0.159.3

# Codex credentials. Must be a regular non-symlink file, mode 0600, owned by
# the launching user.
CODEX_AUTH_JSON_PATH=/home/YOU/.codex/auth.json
# Claude Code runs (launch/flux-moe-ag/run.sh --agent claude-code): a 0600 file
# holding one long-lived OAuth token from `claude setup-token`.
#CLAUDE_OAUTH_TOKEN_FILE=/home/YOU/.config/claude-oauth.token


########################################
# Custom model API (optional)
########################################

# Run Codex against an OpenAI-compatible endpoint instead of the ChatGPT
# auth.json session: a self-hosted DeepSeek behind sglang/vLLM, for example.
# The endpoint must serve /v1/responses (Codex has no chat wire API).
# The key lives in a mode-0600 file; MODEL may then be any id it serves and
# the task scripts skip the auth.json requirement.
#MODEL_API_BASE_URL=http://<endpoint-host>:<port>/v1
#MODEL_API_KEY_FILE=/home/YOU/.config/mlsysforge/model-api.key
#MODEL=<model-id>


########################################
# LLM integrity review (mandatory, docs/LLM_JUDGE.md)
########################################

# Before the GPU Judge runs, a reviewer agent (Codex or Claude Code from an
# agent runtime) inspects each submission in a CPU-only container built from
# the task's Judge image and decides PASS / VIOLATION: did the agent stay
# inside the task's required scope, or circumvent it? It never grades
# quality. enforce (default: reject violations before any GPU work and tell
# the agent why) | shadow (record only) | off -- the last two for debugging.
# Unset runtime/credentials fall back to SFORGE_AGENT_RUNTIME_DIR and
# CODEX_AUTH_JSON_PATH; a dedicated auth.json is recommended.
# Required: the launchers refuse to start unless SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_MODE=enforce
# is set and SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_MODEL names the reviewer's model.
SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_MODE=enforce
# The reviewer's model id (left empty here, the launchers refuse to start until it is set):
SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_MODEL=
# agent (default): the containerised reviewer agent; api: one chat request.
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_ENGINE=agent
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_AGENT=codex
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_AGENT_RUNTIME_DIR=/path/to/agent_runtimes/codex-0.159.3
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_CODEX_AUTH_JSON=/home/YOU/.codex/auth.json
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_REASONING_EFFORT=high
# Or an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (serving /v1/responses for Codex) instead
# of auth.json:
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_API_BASE_URL=http://<endpoint-host>:<port>/v1
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_API_KEY_FILE=/home/YOU/.config/mlsysforge/model-api.key
# Review container: judge (default) or work image; isolated (default: internal
# network + allowlisted egress sidecar) or bridge (open egress, debugging).
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_IMAGE=judge
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_NETWORK=isolated
# Extra HTTPS hosts the reviewer may reach (comma-separated).
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_EGRESS_ALLOW=
# admit (default): an unavailable reviewer lets the submission through;
# block: it ends the submission as an infrastructure error.
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_ON_ERROR=admit
# Independent reviews per submission and the confidence a violation needs.
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_VOTES=1
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.7
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_REVIEW_TIMEOUT=1800
# Review sandboxes alive at once (a slot is held for a whole review).
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_CONCURRENCY=2
# Review container size for tasks without a deployment profile; tasks with
# one use its review size (2 CPU / 4Gi, see SFORGE_RESOURCE_PROFILE below).
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_CPU_LIMIT=4
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_MEM_LIMIT=16g
# Tell agents (enforce mode) that submissions are scope-reviewed.
#SFORGE_LLM_JUDGE_ANNOUNCE=1


########################################
# Networking
########################################

# Work containers cannot reach a proxy bound to the host loopback: inside the
# container 127.0.0.1 is the container itself, so every request fails with
# "connection refused" and a long run burns its budget reconnecting. If this
# host reaches the internet through a loopback proxy, republish it on the
# Docker bridge and point these at that address:
#
#   DOCKER0_IP="$(ip -4 addr show docker0 | grep -oP 'inet \K[0-9.]+')"
#   python3 tasks/latest/quant-videogen-cross-model-kv-codec-h100-v4-scratch/scripts/host_proxy_bridge.py \
#     --listen-host "$DOCKER0_IP" --listen-port 19081 &
#
# Leave all three unset on a host with direct internet access. Tasks that run
# their own restricted CONNECT sidecar ignore these.
#SFORGE_HTTP_PROXY=http://172.17.0.1:19081
#SFORGE_HTTPS_PROXY=http://172.17.0.1:19081
#SFORGE_NO_PROXY=host.docker.internal,localhost,127.0.0.1,172.17.0.1


########################################
# Defaults for a run (every one is also a run.sh flag)
########################################

# (Comments must be on their own line: text after a value becomes part of it.)
# --model MODEL_ID
#MODEL=<model-id>
# --effort max|ultra|xhigh|high|medium|low (some task scripts accept only max to high)
#REASONING_EFFORT=max
# --hours N / --timeout SECONDS
#TASK_TIMEOUT=3600
# defaults to the pin in launch/common.sh
#CODEX_CLI_VERSION=0.159.3

# GPU placement. Single-GPU-pair tasks read WORK_GPU/JUDGE_GPU. The dual-H100
# tasks (sdv2-pipeline, qwen3-orpo, qwen3-gkd) run Work on one
# NVLink pair and the Judge on another, four distinct GPUs, and by default never pause
# Work. <P>_GPU_INDICES is the Work pair (default 0,1; --work-gpus) and
# <P>_JUDGE_GPU_INDICES the Judge pair (default 2,3; --judge-gpus), or
# `shared` to run the Judge on the Work pair and pause Work during each Judge
# round (--shared-gpus; --gpus A,B is a shared run on A,B). A Work pair set
# here without its Judge pair still gets the default Judge pair 2,3.
#WORK_GPU=0
#JUDGE_GPU=1
#JUDGE_PORT=18096
#GKD_GPU_INDICES=0,1
#GKD_JUDGE_GPU_INDICES=2,3
#SDV2_GPU_INDICES=4,5
#SDV2_JUDGE_GPU_INDICES=6,7
# Flux (flux-moe-ag) holds eight GPUs with peer access between every pair; Work
# and the Judge share them and Work is paused for each Judge round (see
# "Flux: eight GPUs" in launch/README.md). FLUXMOE_GPU_INDICES names the eight.
#FLUXMOE_GPU_INDICES=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7
# ORPO v4 also takes each pair's matching UUIDs; without them they are looked
# up with nvidia-smi.
#ORPO_GPU_INDICES=4,5
#ORPO_GPU_UUIDS=GPU-<uuid-of-index-4>,GPU-<uuid-of-index-5>
#ORPO_JUDGE_GPU_INDICES=6,7
#ORPO_JUDGE_GPU_UUIDS=GPU-<uuid-of-index-6>,GPU-<uuid-of-index-7>

# Host locations of task inputs that are not built from the repository.
# ORPO v4: the HF repository directory of Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B (models--Qwen--Qwen3-1.7B,
# not its snapshot) and the two frozen data roots (directories 0711, files o+r).
#ORPO_MODEL_HOST_PATH=/path/to/hf/hub/models--Qwen--Qwen3-1.7B
#ORPO_DATA_HOST_ROOT=/path/to/qwen3-orpo/tldr_preference_v1
#ORPO_PRIVATE_DATA_HOST_ROOT=/path/to/qwen3-orpo/tldr_preference_cross_v4
# StreamDiffusionV2 v2: the staged asset root (weights/clips/embeddings/wheels/...).
#SDV2_ASSETS_ROOT=/path/to/sdv2

# Set to 1 only for a run that deliberately keeps no replayable candidates.
#SFORGE_VERSION_STORE_OPTIONAL=1

# Where to look for a store when SFORGE_VERSION_STORE_ROOT is unset:
# colon-separated absolute paths, tried in order. Only stores that register
# the task being launched are eligible, and two eligible stores fail closed
# rather than picking one. Defaults to a few conventional names beside the
# checkout, so set this when the store lives elsewhere.
#SFORGE_VERSION_STORE_SEARCH_PATH=/srv/mlsysforge/stores/main:/srv/mlsysforge/stores/archive


########################################
# CPU pinning (optional, off by default)
########################################

# Pin every Work and Judge container to the CPUs local to its own GPU(s) and
# bind its memory to that NUMA node. SForge derives the slice from sysfs at
# each container start: one whole L3 group per GPU when the node's L3 groups
# divide evenly among its GPUs, else equal contiguous whole-core chunks; SMT
# siblings stay together and a dual-GPU container gets the union. The slice
# is trimmed to the task's CPU budget. Grammar: off | auto | CPULIST[@NODELIST].
# Also a run.sh/replay.sh flag (--cpuset auto|off|8-11,40-43@0), which is the
# safer route: a value here reaches every launcher that loads this file,
# including
# concurrent-serving (stays unpinned, but its records and replay identity
# change). Opt one launch out with --cpuset off or SFORGE_CPUSET=off in the
# environment. See docs/CPU_AFFINITY.md.
#SFORGE_CPUSET=auto
# Per-role overrides of SFORGE_CPUSET, e.g. pin Work but leave Judge unpinned.
#SFORGE_WORK_CPUSET=auto
#SFORGE_JUDGE_CPUSET=off
# bind (default): cpuset_mems = the slice's NUMA nodes; none: pin CPUs only.
#SFORGE_CPUSET_MEMS=bind
# CPUs kept out of the automatic slices for host daemons (default: none).
# A reserve shrinks the slices on its node: on a two-socket 8-GPU host, 0,32
# can leave each node-0 GPU 6 CPUs, below the 8/16-CPU task budgets, so those
# containers are refused unless SFORGE_CPUSET_UNDERSIZE=allow.
#SFORGE_CPUSET_RESERVE=0,32
# refuse (default): a container whose CPU budget exceeds its slice does not
# start; allow: run it on the
# smaller slice anyway. Unset, a resource-profile quota above the slice is
# pinned to the slice when that still holds the task's own CPU count.
#SFORGE_CPUSET_UNDERSIZE=refuse


########################################
# Container sizes
########################################

# pyromind (default): local Docker Work, Judge and review containers take
# the CPU and memory listed for the task in sforge/harness/resource_profiles.json
# (one entry per released task: the sizes its README states) instead of the
# --work/--judge-cpu/mem-limit values the task scripts pass. native: keep the
# task's own limits. flux-moe-ag always keeps its own.
#SFORGE_RESOURCE_PROFILE=pyromind


########################################
# Task-specific host resources
########################################

# concurrent-agent-serving: an operator-provided model-serving origin plus the
# nonce source and the two baseline-evidence files. See that task's README.
#KVBENCH_VLLM_BASE_URL=http://172.17.0.1:18000
#SFORGE_KVBENCH_NONCE_SOURCE=/path/to/v24.nonces
#KVBENCH_HIDDEN_BASELINE_PATH=/path/to/hidden-direct.json
#KVBENCH_PUBLIC_BASELINE_PATH=/path/to/public-direct.json

# llada: local model repository.
#LLADA_MODEL_REPO=/path/to/LLaDA-8B-Instruct

# quant-videogen: the model and evaluation-input tree. Default: the one its assets/fetch.sh
# assembles at <INFRATHON_ASSETS_ROOT>/quant-videogen-cross-model-kv-codec-h100-v4-scratch/artifact-root.
#QVG_ARTIFACT_ROOT=/path/to/quant-videogen/artifact-root

# Miles task family (tasks/latest/miles-*). scripts/miles_common/host_config.py reads these
# keys from this file too; `python3 scripts/miles_common/host_config.py show` prints what
# each resolves to and where from. The per-task roots default to the Miles /data layout
# under MILES_DATA_ROOT (models/miles-*-assets, mlsysforge/*); set one only to override it.
# With INFRATHON_ASSETS_ROOT in the environment, the task data comes from the fetched assets
# (tasks/latest/<task>/assets/fetch.sh) instead.
# Scratch must be on a large disk that is not the root filesystem (runs write hundreds of GB).
# SForge checkout whose .venv/bin/python and sforge/ run the task (default: this checkout).
#HARNESS_ROOT=/path/to/harness-root
# radixark/miles clone containing commit 78527b9102b3 (git archive source).
#MILES_UPSTREAM=/path/to/miles-upstream
# radixark/miles_diffusion clone containing commit 29fde6ee (git archive source).
#MD_UPSTREAM=/path/to/md-upstream
# root holding models/miles-*-assets and mlsysforge/* (the Miles /data layout).
#MILES_DATA_ROOT=/path/to/miles-data-root
# large, non-root-disk directory for run and build scratch (hundreds of GB per run).
#MILES_SCRATCH_ROOT=/path/to/miles-scratch-root
# Hugging Face hub cache holding the pinned model repos.
#MILES_HF_CACHE=/path/to/miles-hf-cache
# initial Megatron checkpoint (Qwen3-1.7B torch_dist) (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/models/miles-opcd-assets/megatron).
#OPCD_MEGATRON_INIT=/path/to/opcd-megatron-init
# model cache for OPCD (default MILES_HF_CACHE).
#OPCD_HF_CACHE=/path/to/opcd-hf-cache
# OPCD v3 root: assets/task-v3/{public,private,trees,qual} rebuilt from MedMCQA.
#OPCD_V3_ROOT=/path/to/opcd-v3
# OPCD v3 task data, qualification trees and archives (default <OPCD_V3_ROOT>/assets/task-v3).
#OPCD_ASSETS_V3=/path/to/opcd-v3/assets/task-v3
# OPD v2 (math) task data (public/, private/).
#OPD_ASSETS_V2=/path/to/opd-assets-v2
# initial Megatron checkpoint (shared with OPCD) (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/models/miles-opcd-assets/megatron).
#OPD_MEGATRON_INIT=/path/to/opd-megatron-init
# model cache for OPD (default MILES_HF_CACHE).
#OPD_HF_CACHE=/path/to/opd-hf-cache
# ALFWorld task data (public/, private/) (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/models/miles-alfworld-assets/task-v1).
#ALFW_ASSETS=/path/to/alfw-assets
# initial Megatron checkpoint (Qwen3-4B torch_dist) (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/models/miles-alfworld-assets/megatron).
#ALFW_MEGATRON_INIT=/path/to/alfw-megatron-init
# model cache for ALFWorld (default MILES_HF_CACHE).
#ALFW_HF_CACHE=/path/to/alfw-hf-cache
# SD3.5-M weights and teachers (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/models/miles-diffusion-assets).
#MDOPD_ASSETS=/path/to/mdopd-assets
# SD3.5-M v2 data root: scorers/ (PickScore_v1, CLIP-ViT-H-14-processor), public-02/root, private-02 (root-owned, 0700).
#MDOPD_V2_ROOT=/path/to/mdopd-v2
# SD3.5-M v2 task-metric scorers (default <MDOPD_V2_ROOT>/scorers).
#MDOPD_V2_SCORERS=/path/to/mdopd-v2/scorers
# SD3.5-M v2 public data root (default <MDOPD_V2_ROOT>/public-02/root).
#MDOPD_V2_PUBLIC_DATA=/path/to/mdopd-v2/public-02/root
# SD3.5-M v2 private Judge root (owner not the container agent uid, mode 0700) (default <MDOPD_V2_ROOT>/private-02).
#MDOPD_V2_PRIVATE_DATA=/path/to/mdopd-v2/private-02
# number of physical cores local to the GPU pair that SD3.5-M Work and Judge are pinned to (unset: 24).
#MDOPD_CPU_CORES=16
# Wan2.2-TI2V-5B, HPSv3, Qwen2-VL-7B (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/models/miles-diffusion-wan).
#MDWAN_ASSETS=/path/to/mdwan-assets
# Wan2.2 public data root (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/mlsysforge/md-wandance/public/v1).
#MDWAN_PUBLIC_DATA=/path/to/mdwan-public-data
# Wan2.2 private Judge root (owner not the container agent uid, mode 0700) (default <MILES_DATA_ROOT>/mlsysforge/md-wandance/private/v2).
#MDWAN_PRIVATE_DATA=/path/to/mdwan-private-data
# number of physical cores local to the GPU pair that Wan2.2 Work and Judge are pinned to (unset: 24).
#MDWAN_CPU_CORES=16
# build records of scripts/miles_base_images/build.sh (default: outputs/miles-base-images).
#MILES_BASE_IMAGE_RECORDS=/path/to/miles-base-image-records
